  <model metaid="meta_empagliflozin_liver" id="empagliflozin_liver" name="Model for the hepatic metabolism of empagliflozin." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for the hepatic metabolism of empagliflozin.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Empagliflozin is taken up into the hepatocytes by OATP1B1 and OATP1B3
and glucuronidated by UGT2B7, UGT1A3, UGT1A8 and UGT1A9 to the 2-O-, 3-O-
and 6-O-glucuronides (EG), which are released into the plasma and
excreted in the urine; no glucuronide is found in the feces [Chen2015a].</li>
          <li>The hepatic clearance is a first-order clearance of the plasma of the
liver: the uptake is the rate determining step of the low permeable
empagliflozin (<code>f_oatp</code>), the glucuronidation (<code>f_ugt</code>) is far below its
Km. It scales with the volume of the liver tissue, so with the tissue
loss in cirrhosis.</li>
          <li>The exposure rises with the Child-Pugh class (AUC ratio 1.23, 1.47, 1.75
[Macha2014b]); with rifampicin (single dose, inhibition of OATP1B1/1B3)
the AUC rises by 35 % [Macha2014].</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
